             "children": [
              "Claude starts caching this conversation with your first message, and keeps it for an hour after it last used it. While it's warm, each message re-reads it from the cache, which costs far less. Once it's cold, the next message writes it all into the cache again. Compact shrinks the conversation, so both cost less."
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "Text",
             "props": {
              "bold": false
             },
             "children": [
              "Auto cache pings a background copy of the conversation 10 minutes before the cache would go cold, which keeps it hot without adding anything to the chat. A ping costs about a twentieth of a rewrite, so it stops after 20 in a row (about 16 hours away) and starts again when you send a message."
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "Text",
             "props": {
              "bold": false
             },
             "children": [
              "Auto compact compacts the conversation once it passes 400k tokens, right after Claude's reply. Past that size every message costs more and Claude misses more of what's in it; Claude Code's own auto-compact would wait until about 830k."
